  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 300 AM EDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nEarly morning RAP analysis and GOES WV imagery show zonal flow \nacross the northern tier of the U.S. A closed low over Hudson Bay is \nstacked well over a eastward tracking sfc low at 987 mb, draping a \ncold front across the western UP. With dry air and weak forcing, \nskies remain mostly clear. The slackening pressure gradient \ncontinues to taper off winds through this morning as temps approach \nthe mid 30s to mid 40s. \n\nHigh pressure takes hold overhead today, yielding calm and quiet \nweather in the wake of the weak cold front. Temps will be 5-15 F \nabove normal in the mid 50s to mid 60s under few high clouds and \nplenty of sunshine. While not a deep mixed layer, cold Tds aloft \nmixing down will yield low RHs in the western UP down into the upper \n20s to upper 30s. That said, wind will be quite light (gusts mainly \n10 mph or less) preventing elevated wildfire conditions. More \nfavorable radiative cooling tonight yields lows mostly in the upper \n20s to 30s. High pressure moves to Quebec for Tuesday, but ridging \nremains extended overhead yielding similar weather to today. That \nsaid, minimum RH will be higher in the 40s and 50s. Temps climb well \ninto the 60s on Wednesday ahead of a cold front. Limited moisture \nand weak forcing suggests cloud cover, but no precip will accompany \nthis front. \n\nFrom there, high pressure dominates the rest of the work week \nforecast. Temps remain 5-15 F above normal with highs in the \nupper 50s to upper 60s and lows in the 30s to upper 40s. The \nnext chance (15-30%) comes late weekend as a stronger cold front\nwith better moisture sweeps across the area. Although precip \nchances are low, breezy southerly winds are likely (50-70% \nchance) on Saturday, frequently gusting in the 20-30 mph range \nwhere downslope flow is favored. A cool down closer to normal is\nanticipated in the wake of the cold front early next week, but \ncurrent trends favor above normal temps continuing through the \nend of the month captured in the CPC 8-14 day outlooks (~65% \nchance).",
